<title>BRAZIL: Brazil non-ferrous metals - April statistics.</title>
<headline>Brazil non-ferrous metals - April statistics.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production of Brazilian non-ferrous metals in April 1997 and consumption, imports and exports in January/April compared with 1996 were as follows, said the Secretariat of Mines and Metallurgy.</p>
<p>All figures are in tonnes.</p>
<p>  METAL		 PRODUCTION(APRIL)  CONSUMPTION (JAN/APR)</p>
<p>			  1997	 1996	     1997	 1996</p>
<p> Aluminium	   99,000     97,700	 138,490    150,024</p>
<p> Lead			 0	    0	     n/a	  n/a</p>
<p> Copper		15,070     14,450	  86,672     63,553</p>
<p> Tin		    1,197	1,513	     761	2,299</p>
<p> Magnesium		n/a	   25	     n/a	  n/a</p>
<p> Nickel		 1,224	1,463	  (1,811)     1,444</p>
<p> Zinc		  14,582     16,151	  48,784     39,238</p>
<p> METAL		  EXPORTS (APRIL)	   IMPORTS (JAN/APR)</p>
<p>			  197	 1996		1997	 1996</p>
<p> Aluminium	  285,328    284,391	  50,074     32,480</p>
<p> Lead			59	1,501	  15,363	5,014</p>
<p> Copper		17,282     24,736	  54,994     50,564</p>
<p> Tin		    4,494	3,651		23	    7</p>
<p> Magnesium		 83	  983	   2,191	  607</p>
<p> Nickel		 1,891	1,701	   2,892	2,437</p>
<p> Zinc		  11,453     24,704	     688	2,849</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
</text>
